ype":"Answer","text":"This symptom is usually a sign of worn-down friction material, which leaves the metal backing plate contacting the rotor. When this occurs, there may be wear or score marks on your rotors. Grinding may also be caused by contamination of friction material or misaligned pads due to worn out hardware. If grinding occurs, stop by our nearest location for a consultation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where Can I Schedule a Brake Repair Near Me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can get your vehicle’s brakes repaired or replaced at most automotive shops, including our local locations. Find a Service Center"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Does Brake Fluid Do?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brake fluid is responsible for moving hydraulic components within a braking system. It is a non-compressible fluid that allows force from your foot to apply pressure on the brakes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where Does Brake Fluid Go?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brake fluid goes from the master cylinder (connected to the brake pedal) to the caliper or wheel cylinder at the wheels.\nLearn more about brake fluids in our Brake Fluid & Flush Service"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Long Do Brake Pads Last?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There are many factors that may determine the longevity of brakes, including environmental factors like mountain driving, highway driving, or stop-and-go traffic. Driver habits can also be a factor; do you gradually stop at a light, or stop with more pedal force? Additionally, the quality of the brake material can also be a factor."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Does an Anti-Lock Braking System Mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Anti-lock braking systems (ABS) are designed to help prevent wheels from locking up, enabling the driver to make a controlled stop."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a Brake Caliper?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A brake caliper is the part of the brake system located at the wheel that applies pressure on the piston which, in turn, pushes the brake pad against the rotor to slow or stop the vehicle."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When to Replace Your Brake Pads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brake pads should be replaced when there is 3 millimeters (mm) or less of friction material left, or when the wear indicator is activated."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Color is Brake Fluid?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brake fluid is a clear liquid with a hint of yellow. If it appears dark in color, it may need to be replaced due to contamination and should be tested."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"WebSite","url":"index.html","potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"index.html?q={search_term_string"},"query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"Service","name":"Brake Service & Repair","brand":{"@type":"Brand","name":"Goodyear"},"description":"A vehicle’s braking system contains components that need to be inspected, repaired or even replaced. The technicians at our locations will inspect or replace brake pads or shoes, plus resurface rotors as needed. Schedule an appointment today.","url":"-us/services/brake-service-repair_211129/index.html","provider":{"@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"Goodyear"}}</script><!--$--><!--$--><!--/$--><div class="Services relative min-h-screen"><!--$--><!--/$--><div><div class="opacity-100"><div class="analytics-event-listener contents"></div></div><nav role="navigation" aria-label="Jump Navigation" class="w-full shadow-pdp-jumpnav bg-[#f4f4f4] fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50
