; height: 0px;"><div class="flex flex-col gap-4"><div class="text-black last:mb-0"><p class="paragraph-md text-action-color-secondary !normal-case">Shaking may be caused by an out-of-round brake rotor or brake drum, which you might feel through the brake pedal. Another contributing factor could be a sticking brake caliper with worn out brake hardware, in which case you would feel vibrations through the steering wheel.</p><p class="paragraph-md text-action-color-secondary !normal-case"></p></div></div></div></div><div class="border-t-2 last:border-b-2 text-type-standard  border-background-100 border-background-100" data-open="false" data-qa-id="accordion-item-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-content-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" id="accordion-header-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" class="py-4 pr-6 pl-0 cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center w-full border-none text-left gap-6 capitalize bg-transparent paragraph-lg text-type-standard  border-t-background-100 text-type-standard" data-qa-id="accordion-summary-header-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" data-tracking="{&quot;eventType&quot;:&quot;web.webinteraction.linkClicks&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cta:accordion-container:what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-im-braking&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;other&quot;,&quot;componentType&quot;:&quot;accordion-container&quot;,&quot;componentName&quot;:&quot;accordion-container|accordion-summary&quot;,&quot;componentElement&quot;:&quot;button&quot;,&quot;productListAdds&quot;:false}"><div class="flex flex-col gap-2"><h3 class="heading-xs !normal-case text-type-standard" id="what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-im-braking">What is the Grinding Noise When I’m Braking?</h3></div><span class="transition-transform duration-300 ease-out flex items-center ml-auto"><i class="icon-chevron-down flex justify-center items-center icon-md " aria-hidden="true" data-qa-id="accordion-summary-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3-icon-chevron" style="font-size: 24px; width: 24px; height: 24px; color: currentcolor;"><span class="path1"></span><span class="path2"></span><span class="path3"></span><span class="path4"></span><span class="path5"></span><span class="path6"></span><span class="path7"></span><span class="path8"></span><span class="path9"></span><span class="path10"></span><span class="path11"></span><span class="path12"></span><span class="path13"></span><span class="path14"></span></i></span></button><div id="accordion-content-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="accordion-header-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" class="overflow-hidden transition-[height] duration-300 ease-in pb-0 px-0 pb-6" aria-hidden="true" data-qa-id="accordion-details-_r_3_-what-is-the-grinding-noise-when-i’m-braking?-3" style="overflow: hidden; transition: height 0.3s; display: none; height: 0px;"><div class="flex flex-col gap-4"><div class="text-black last:mb-0"><p class="paragraph-md text-action-color-secondary !normal-case">This symptom is usually a sign of worn-down friction material, which leaves the metal backing plate contacting the rotor. When this occurs, there may be wear or score marks on your rotors. Grinding may also be caused by contamination of friction material or misaligned pads due to worn out hardware. If grinding occurs, stop by our nearest location for a consultation.</p><p class="paragraph-md text-action-color-secondary !normal-case"></p></div></div></div></div><div class="border-t-2 last:border-b-2 text-type-standard  border-background-100 border-background-100" data-open="false" data-qa-id="accordion-item-_r_3_-where-can-i-schedule-a-brake-repair-near-me?-4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-content-_r_3_-where-can-i-schedule-a-brake-repair-near-me?-4" id="accordion-header-_r_3_-where-can-i-schedule-a-brake-rep